      "value": "used",
      "quote": "Tests of respiratory and muscular function were performed. Baseline arterial blood gases (ABG) showed mild hypoxemia (PaO2 64 mmHg) with normocapnia (PaCO2 42 mmHg) and pH of 7.44. A nocturnal cardiorespiratory polygraphy with capnography showed a substantially normal respiratory function, with regular breathing, mild hypoxemia (mean oxygen saturation, SpO2, 96.5%, with lowest value of 88%) and normal transcutaneous PCO2 values (highest transcutaneous PCO2 of 45 mmHg). - Spirometric values were normal, excluding restrictive or obstructive syndromes. Tests of muscle strength tests were within normal range, excluding the most common neuromuscular disorders. Laryngoscopy was unremarkable. Ultrasound and fluoroscopy evaluation during a sniff maneuver confirmed that diaphragm excursions were normal.",
